1. PURPOSE
Stack 52.0 defines the application architecture required to implement the Global Geospatial Intelligence, Mapping & Earth Data Integration Architecture established by Stack 51.0.
Stack 51.0 establishes the geographic architecture.
Stack 52.0 establishes how that architecture becomes an operational OneDraft application capability.
The system shall therefore progress from:
51.0
GLOBAL GEOSPATIAL ARCHITECTURE
        ↓
52.0
GLOBAL GEOSPATIAL APPLICATION
        ↓
SPATIAL REPOSITORY
        ↓
WORLD MODEL
        ↓
ONEDRAFT PROJECT INTEGRATION
Stack 52.0 establishes the application-layer implementation through which geographic information becomes accessible to OneDraft projects, Aria, the project model, the CAD/BIM environment, the documentation system and future global Earth-data systems.

2. SYSTEM OBJECTIVE
The objective of Stack 52.0 is to transform the geographic architecture established in Stack 51.0 into a persistent application capability capable of:
Registering geographic locations
Registering existing structures
Georeferencing OneDraft projects
Connecting projects to geographic context
Connecting existing-world information to projects
Maintaining spatial relationships
Maintaining temporal states
Maintaining source provenance
Synchronizing authorized GIS information
Supporting geographic search
Supporting spatial analysis
Supporting Aria geospatial operations
Maintaining a global project index
Providing a foundation for future Earth-data applications
The application shall be capable of expanding from individual project locations to a global spatial repository without requiring architectural replacement.

