75. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
Stack 52.0 shall preserve the following invariants:
Geographic Identity: Every georeferenced project has a persistent spatial identity.
Provenance: External information remains attributable to its source.
Temporal Integrity: Historical states remain distinguishable.
Authority: External GIS information does not automatically override OneDraft project state.
Determinism: Spatial calculations use deterministic services.
AI Separation: Aria interprets and orchestrates but does not replace authoritative spatial computation.
Security: Geographic location does not override access control.
Scalability: The application can grow from project scale to planetary scale.
